499 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 109 0 R
/E (In August 2025, I participated in a rural planning internship with a rural fieldwork association in Meinong District, Kaohsiung City, where I resided in the village for one month and closely engaged with local life. Through field surveys, I examined local resource allocation, conducted resident interviews, and took part in a farmland water-retention project. While Meinong is a high-quality agricultural area, it also faces challenges such as resource misallocation and degradation of rural landscapes. Contrary to my prior assumptions, I came to recognize that some rural areas are not poor but instead exhibit relatively high income levels with limited investment channels. This insight motivated me to further study rural and local economic growth from a financial perspective.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
